      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "LOCATION\r\n\r\nThe subject property is located just to the east of Lecanvey village, approximately 11 kms west of Westport Town Centre and 9 kms east of Louisburgh. This is a small coastal village located on the southern shores of Clew Bay. Local amenities include Lecanvey Beach and Pier, an RC Church, Community Centre and Staunton's pub. The property is positioned on the north side of the R335 with direct road frontage. Murrisk Village and Croagh Patrick are close by together with Campbell's pub and The Tavern Bar & Restaurant.\r\n\r\nIn a wider context, Westport is an immensely popular coastal town located on the inner shores of Clew Bay and on the Wild Atlantic Way. There are a number of significant employers including AbbVie Pharmaceuticals and Portwest. Westport is well connected with road and rail infrastructure, being on the N5, N59 and main Westport to Dublin railway line.\r\n \r\nDESCRIPTION\r\n\r\nThe property comprises of a modest 2 / 3 bedroom bungalow, we understand dating from c. 1940. Construction is either mass concrete or rendered block with single glazed teak windows under a pitched roof. Extending to about 65sq.m, to the front is a small, glazed porch leading into a central hallway. The living room is to the front with 2 to 3 bedrooms one of which is currently used as an office. The kitchen and bathroom are located towards the rear of the property.\r\n \r\nExternally, the property has a small enclosed rear garden and on-site parking for a single car. The total plot area is 800 sq.m / 0.08 Ha (0.197 Acres) which is configured in a rectangular shape.\r\n\r\nFEATURES:\r\n\r\n•Desirable coastal location on south side of Clew Bay\r\n•Comprises a small 2/3 bedroom roadside bungalow extending to c.65sq.m (700sq ft)\r\n•Property is in need of some refurbishment but is habitable\r\n•Has been vacant for several years and should qualify for Vacant House/Derelict Property Grants subject to eligibility\r\n\r\nACCOMMODATION COMPRISES: \r\n \r\nGROUND FLOOR\r\n\r\nENTRANCE PORCH:0.9m x 2.94m\r\nTeak single glazed window, teak door, timber panelling to walls and ceiling\r\n\r\nLIVING ROOM:3.29m x 2.86m\r\nLiving room, open fire, carpeted floors\r\n\r\nDINING ROOM / LIVING ROOM :4.18m x 2.93m\r\nCarpeted floor, open fireplace, electric fire, part timber panelled ceiling. Hotpress\r\n\r\nKITCHEN:3.16m x 1.65m\r\nGalley style, timber floor and eye level units, stainless steel sink, tiled splashback, Formica worktop\r\n\r\nHALLWAY:7.51m x 0.92m\r\nSkylight, carpeted floor\r\n\r\n \r\nSTUDY / OFFICE:2.89m x 2.78m\r\nLino floor, Formica counter, extensive areas of shelving\r\n\r\nSTOREROOM :1.9m x 1.66m\r\n\r\n\r\nBATHROOM:2.7m x 2.02m\r\nLino floor, electric corner shower with glazed surround, wc, whb\r\n\r\nBEDROOM (1):3.33m x 3.16m\r\nCarpeted floor, fitted wardrobes\r\n\r\nBEDROOM (2):3.0m x 3.13m\r\nCarpeted floor, fitted wardrobes\r\n\r\nTITLE\r\n\r\nRegistered Freehold title registered within Folio MY6579F\r\n\r\nSERVICES\r\n\r\nThe property may have the following services:-\r\n\r\nSewerage-Septic Tank (this is in an adjoining owner's field)\r\nWater-May be connected to Group Water Scheme but there is now mains \r\nwater available at this location\r\nElectricity-Mains \r\nTelecoms-Unknown\r\nHeating- Oil fired central heating\r\n\r\n\r\nGUIDE PRICE 175,000\r\n\r\nVIEWINGS\r\n\r\nStrictly by appointment only. Please contact O'Toole & Co. on 098 28000 or info@tot.ie.\r\n\r\nDIRECTIONS\r\n\r\nThe property is located just to the east of Lecanvey village on the main Westport to Louisburgh Road. Follow google maps directions for Eircode F28N677."
